{"duration_api_ms":84020,"stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"f8d23bbf-8809-4115-83fa-d33b4cb25e8e","total_cost_usd":0.515251,"usage":{"input_tokens":22,"cache_creation_input_tokens":38309,"cache_read_input_tokens":354955,"output_tokens":6885,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":1234},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":38309,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":771,"cache_read_input_tokens":41753,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2536,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2536},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-opus-5-5":{"inputTokens":22,"outputTokens":6885,"cacheReadInputTokens":354955,"cacheCreationInputTokens":38309,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.515251,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":128000,"thinkingTokens":1234,"canonicalModel":"claude-opus-5-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subagent_stats":{"spawned":0,"requested":{"background":0,"foreground":0,"unset":0},"started_in_background":0,"max_depth":0,"spawned_by_subagents":0,"completed":0,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{}},"is_error":false,"num_turns":17,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"The build stage for **catalogue-title** has stopped with a question for you, because I couldn't apply the judge's fix without breaking other tests.\n\nThis was the second build round. The first round's change still stands and the story's behaviour is met: the catalogue page's title reads exactly \"Product Catalog\". The judge approved that, but found one defect in the test: the page object finds the `<h1>` heading by its ARIA role. `project/product.md` says every element a test uses must carry a `data-test` attribute.\n\nThe judge's fix was to add `data-test=\"catalog-heading\"` to the `<h1>`. That breaks two integration tests that match the heading's exact markup:\n- `tests/DcaShop.IntegrationTests/ProductPageTest.cs:70` looks for the literal `<h1>Our Products</h1>`.\n- `tests/DcaShop.IntegrationTests/ProductPageTest.cs:85` uses the pattern `<h1>([^<]*)</h1>`.\n\nThe plan says those tests must not change, and the build stage may not change a test to make it pass. I made the fix, spotted the conflict, and undid both edits, so the working tree is exactly as round 1 left it. I worked this out by reading the tests; I didn't run the integration suite with the attribute in place.\n\nThe question is in `.agents/factory/decisions/catalogue-title-01.md` with four options:\n1. Add the attribute and loosen the two integration tests so they match the heading's text. This changes tests from another story and needs the same change in the Java template.\n2. **Recommended:** remove the heading check from the browser test. The integration tests already check \"Our Products\". No markup changes and nothing to sync to Java, but it departs from the plan.\n3. Wrap the heading in a `<div data-test=\"catalog-heading\">`. Every test stays green, but it adds markup only for testing and differs from the Java template.\n4. Keep the role-based lookup and record it as an exception for this one heading.\n\n`tasks/catalogue-title/build.md` records all of this, including the pointer to the decision. I didn't re-run the checks this round because no code changed in the end; round 1's results still apply and all were green. I applied `dca-discipline` in this session to every file I wrote.\n\nYou can answer with `/factory-decisions`, and the build stage then runs again.","ttft_ms":3327,"type":"result","duration_ms":91006,"uuid":"7e3ed288-e60b-4d5c-a1c8-eea71460d580","ttft_stream_ms":1960,"time_to_request_ms":41,"first_content_frame_ms":1960,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
